2026-08-05 14:42:23 | INFO     | main_agent.<module>:31 | Main Agent response: {'messages': [HumanMessage(content='Create a post endpoint in flask.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='fa75800a-76e0-4ba7-8c9c-cf1744bfd187'), AIMessage(content='', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model': 'qwen3-coder:30b', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T04:33:52.4476392Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 1158784852800, 'load_duration': 186767530800, 'prompt_eval_count': 2861, 'prompt_eval_duration': 929515335000, 'eval_count': 65, 'eval_duration': 42034627000, 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'qwen3-coder:30b', 'model_provider': 'ollama'}, id='lc_run--019fd021-56b4-7c73-96c2-fd3ff384390a-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'task', 'args': {'description': 'Create a POST endpoint in Flask that accepts JSON data, validates it, and returns a response. The endpoint should handle common HTTP status codes and include proper error handling.', 'subagent_type': 'API_Manager'}, 'id': '1ae2ec27-0f08-48cf-a154-bbc76e13c015', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2861, 'output_tokens': 65, 'total_tokens': 2926}), ToolMessage(content="I've analyzed your request and created a comprehensive Flask application with a POST endpoint that handles JSON data validation and appropriate HTTP status codes. The solution includes:\n\n1. A complete Flask application (app.py) with:\n   - POST /users endpoint\n   - JSON validation using marshmallow schema\n   - Required field checking (name, email, age)\n   - Data type validation (email format, age as integer)\n   - Custom validation (age must be positive)\n   - Proper HTTP status codes (201, 400, 422, 500)\n\n2. Supporting files:\n   - requirements.txt with Flask and marshmallow dependencies\n   - README.md with documentation\n   - run.sh shell script to execute the application\n   - run_app.py for application execution with error handling\n   - final_test.py for verification\n\nThe implementation handles all common scenarios including valid requests that return 201 Created, invalid requests due to missing fields returning 422 Unprocessable Entity, incorrect Content-Type returning 400 Bad Request, and unexpected errors returning 500 Internal Server Error.\n\nTo run this application:\n1. Install dependencies: `pip install -r requirements.txt`\n2. Execute the application: `python app.py` or `./run.sh`\n3. Test with curl commands as shown in the README\n\nThe solution provides structured JSON responses for all scenarios and follows REST API best practices for error handling and status code usage.", name='task', id='fa9d5e28-a732-45a0-a6f0-90e7df07dc41', tool_call_id='1ae2ec27-0f08-48cf-a154-bbc76e13c015'), AIMessage(content="I've analyzed your request and created a comprehensive Flask application with a POST endpoint that handles JSON data validation and appropriate HTTP status codes. The solution includes:\n\n1. A complete Flask application (app.py) with:\n   - POST /users endpoint\n   - JSON validation using marshmallow schema\n   - Required field checking (name, email, age)\n   - Data type validation (email format, age as integer)\n   - Custom validation (age must be positive)\n   - Proper HTTP status codes (201, 400, 422, 500)\n\n2. Supporting files:\n   - requirements.txt with Flask and marshmallow dependencies\n   - README.md with documentation\n   - run.sh shell script to execute the application\n   - run_app.py for application execution with error handling\n   - final_test.py for verification\n\nThe implementation handles all common scenarios including valid requests that return 201 Created, invalid requests due to missing fields returning 422 Unprocessable Entity, incorrect Content-Type returning 400 Bad Request, and unexpected errors returning 500 Internal Server Error.\n\nTo run this application:\n1. Install dependencies: `pip install -r requirements.txt`\n2. Execute the application: `python app.py` or `./run.sh`\n3. Test with curl commands as shown in the README\n\nThe solution provides structured JSON responses for all scenarios and follows REST API best practices for error handling and status code usage.", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model': 'qwen3-coder:30b', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T09:12:23.0082537Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 173780129400, 'load_duration': 292978800, 'prompt_eval_count': 3236, 'prompt_eval_duration': 56377139000, 'eval_count': 299, 'eval_duration': 112339823000, 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'qwen3-coder:30b', 'model_provider': 'ollama'}, id='lc_run--019fd12f-5a05-71d3-9a17-834bfe602c0c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3236, 'output_tokens': 299, 'total_tokens': 3535})], 'files': {'/app.py': {'content': 'from flask import Flask, request, jsonify\nfrom marshmallow import Schema, fields, ValidationError, validates\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n# User schema for validation\nclass UserSchema(Schema):\n    name = fields.Str(required=True)\n    email = fields.Email(required=True)\n    age = fields.Int(required=True)\n    is_active = fields.Bool(missing=False)\n\n    @validates(\'age\')\n    def validate_age(self, value):\n        if value < 0:\n            raise ValidationError(\'Age must be a positive number.\')\n\n# Initialize the schema\nuser_schema = UserSchema()\n\n@app.route(\'/health\', methods=[\'GET\'])\ndef health_check():\n    """Health check endpoint"""\n    return jsonify({\n        "status": "healthy",\n        "message": "Flask JSON validation API is running"\n    }), 200\n\n@app.route(\'/users\', methods=[\'POST\'])\ndef create_user():\n    """Create a new user with validation"""\n    \n    # Check if Content-Type is application/json\n    if request.content_type != \'application/json\':\n        return jsonify({\n            "error": "Content-Type must be application/json",\n            "status_code": 400\n        }), 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Parse JSON data\n        data = request.get_json()\n        \n        # Validate data using marshmallow schema\n        validated_data = user_schema.load(data)\n        \n        # Here you would typically save to a database\n        # For this example, we\'ll just return the validated data\n        \n        response = {\n            "message": "User created successfully",\n            "user": validated_data\n        }\n        \n        return jsonify(response), 201\n        \n    except ValidationError as err:\n        # Handle validation errors (422 Unprocessable Entity)\n        return jsonify({\n            "error": "Validation failed",\n            "details": err.messages,\n            "status_code": 422\n        }), 422\n        \n    except Exception as e:\n        # Handle unexpected server errors (500 Internal Server Error)\n        return jsonify({\n            "error": "Internal server error",\n            "status_code": 500\n        }), 500\n\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\n    app.run(\n        host=\'0.0.0.0\',\n        port=5000,\n        debug=False\n    )', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T05:10:57.554393+00:00', 'modified_at': '2026-08-05T07:44:04.631634+00:00'}, '/requirements.txt': {'content': 'Flask==2.3.3\nmarshmallow==3.20.1\nrequests==2.31.0', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T05:12:14.918198+00:00', 'modified_at': '2026-08-05T06:59:31.082881+00:00'}, '/README.md': {'content': '# Flask JSON Validation API\n\nA simple Flask application with a POST endpoint that accepts JSON data, validates it, and returns appropriate HTTP responses.\n\n## Features\n\n- POST endpoint for creating users\n- JSON data validation with marshmallow\n- Proper HTTP status codes (201 Created, 400 Bad Request, 422 Unprocessable Entity)\n- Error handling for common status codes\n- Structured JSON responses\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### POST /users\n\nCreates a new user with the provided data.\n\n#### Request Body (JSON)\n```json\n{\n    "name": "John Doe",\n    "email": "john@example.com",\n    "age": 30,\n    "is_active": true\n}\n```\n\n#### Valid Fields\n- `name` (string, required)\n- `email` (string, required, must be valid email format)\n- `age` (integer, required)\n- `is_active` (boolean, optional, defaults to false)\n\n#### Success Response (201 Created)\n```json\n{\n    "message": "User created successfully",\n    "user": {\n        "name": "John Doe",\n        "email": "john@example.com",\n        "age": 30,\n        "is_active": true\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Validation Error Response (422 Unprocessable Entity)\n```json\n{\n    "error": "Validation failed",\n    "details": {\n        "name": ["Missing data for required field."],\n        "email": ["Not a valid email address."]\n    },\n    "status_code": 422\n}\n```\n\n#### Bad Request Response (400)\n```json\n{\n    "error": "Content-Type must be application/json",\n    "status_code": 400\n}\n```\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Install dependencies:\n   ```\n   pip install -r requirements.txt\n   ```\n\n2. Run the application:\n   ```\n   python app.py\n   ```\n\n3. The server will start on http://localhost:5000\n\n## Testing\n\nYou can test the endpoint using curl:\n\n```bash\n# Valid request\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:5000/users \\\n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n  -d \'{"name": "John Doe", "email": "john@example.com", "age": 30}\'\n\n# Invalid request (missing required fields)\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:5000/users \\\n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n  -d \'{"name": "John Doe"}\'\n```', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T05:18:51.891123+00:00', 'modified_at': '2026-08-05T05:18:51.891123+00:00'}, '/Dockerfile': {'content': 'FROM python:3.9-slim\n\nWORKDIR /app\n\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\n\nCOPY . .\n\nEXPOSE 5000\n\nCMD ["python", "app.py"]', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T05:27:06.844024+00:00', 'modified_at': '2026-08-05T05:27:06.844024+00:00'}, '/run_app.py': {'content': '#!/usr/bin/env python3\n"""\nScript to run the Flask application with proper error handling\n"""\n\nimport sys\nimport os\nfrom app import app\n\ndef main():\n    try:\n        # Check if we\'re running in a production environment\n        debug_mode = os.environ.get(\'FLASK_DEBUG\', \'False\').lower() == \'true\'\n        \n        print("Starting Flask application...")\n        print(f"Debug mode: {debug_mode}")\n        \n        # Run the Flask app\n        app.run(\n            host=\'0.0.0.0\',\n            port=int(os.environ.get(\'PORT\', 5000)),\n            debug=debug_mode,\n            threaded=True\n        )\n        \n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        print("\\nShutting down application...")\n        sys.exit(0)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f"Error starting application: {e}")\n        sys.exit(1)\n\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\n    main()', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T05:29:46.496735+00:00', 'modified_at': '2026-08-05T05:29:46.496735+00:00'}, '/run.sh': {'content': '#!/bin/bash\n\n# Simple script to run the Flask application\n\necho "Starting Flask application..."\n\n# Install dependencies if not already installed\nif ! pip show flask marshmallow > /dev/null 2>&1; then\n    echo "Installing dependencies..."\n    pip install -r requirements.txt\nfi\n\n# Run the application\npython run_app.py', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T05:49:32.503489+00:00', 'modified_at': '2026-08-05T07:34:48.651552+00:00'}, '/final_test.py': {'content': '#!/usr/bin/env python3\n"""\nFinal verification that the Flask application works correctly\n"""\n\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport requests\nimport json\n\ndef test_application():\n    print("Testing Flask JSON Validation API...")\n    \n    # Start the Flask app in a subprocess\n    try:\n        process = subprocess.Popen([\n            sys.executable, \'app.py\'\n        ], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)\n        \n        # Give the app time to start\n        time.sleep(2)\n        \n        print("1. Testing health endpoint...")\n        response = requests.get(\'http://localhost:5000/health\')\n        if response.status_code == 200:\n            print("   ✓ Health check works")\n        else:\n            print(f"   ✗ Health check failed with status {response.status_code}")\n            return False\n            \n        print("2. Testing valid POST request...")\n        data = {\n            "name": "John Doe",\n            "email": "john@example.com",\n            "age": 30,\n            "is_active": True\n        }\n        response = requests.post(\n            \'http://localhost:5000/users\',\n            json=data,\n            headers={\'Content-Type\': \'application/json\'}\n        )\n        \n        if response.status_code == 201:\n            print("   ✓ Valid POST request works")\n            result = response.json()\n            if "message" in result and "user" in result:\n                print("   ✓ Response structure is correct")\n            else:\n                print("   ✗ Response structure incorrect")\n                return False\n        else:\n            print(f"   ✗ Valid POST request failed with status {response.status_code}")\n            print(f"   Response: {response.text}")\n            return False\n            \n        print("3. Testing invalid POST request (validation error)...")\n        data = {\n            "name": "John Doe"\n        }\n        response = requests.post(\n            \'http://localhost:5000/users\',\n            json=data,\n            headers={\'Content-Type\': \'application/json\'}\n        )\n        \n        if response.status_code == 422:\n            print("   ✓ Invalid POST request properly rejected with 422")\n            result = response.json()\n            if "error" in result and "details" in result:\n                print("   ✓ Error response structure is correct")\n            else:\n                print("   ✗ Error response structure incorrect")\n                return False\n        else:\n            print(f"   ✗ Invalid POST request should have failed with 422, got {response.status_code}")\n            return False\n            \n        print("4. Testing invalid Content-Type...")\n        data = {\n            "name": "John Doe",\n            "email": "john@example.com",\n            "age": 30\n        }\n        response = requests.post(\n            \'http://localhost:5000/users\',\n            json=data,\n            headers={\'Content-Type\': \'text/plain\'}\n        )\n        \n        if response.status_code == 400:\n            print("   ✓ Invalid Content-Type properly rejected with 400")\n        else:\n            print(f"   ✗ Invalid Content-Type should have failed with 400, got {response.status_code}")\n            return False\n            \n        # Stop the Flask app\n        process.terminate()\n        process.wait()\n        \n        print("\\n✓ All tests passed! The Flask application is working correctly.")\n        return True\n        \n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f"✗ Test failed with error: {e}")\n        return False\n\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\n    success = test_application()\n    sys.exit(0 if success else 1)', 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'created_at': '2026-08-05T07:58:22.496444+00:00', 'modified_at': '2026-08-05T07:58:22.496444+00:00'}}}
